- @infra_cap_generous: Generous allotment
- @infra_cap_fair: Fair allotment
- @terms_menu

@infra_cap_generous
title: Generous infrastructure allotment
subtitle: High quotas before cutbacks bite — easier to sell at the table
choose-if: cable_neg_infra_cap = 0
unavailable-subtitle: Infrastructure cap already set.
on-arrival: {!
Q.cableNegEnsureApi()
Q.cable_neg_infra_cap = 1
Q.cableNegReprisalAddEach(Q.CABLE_NEG_REPR_INFRA_GENEROUS_EACH)
!}
go-to: terms_menu

@infra_cap_fair
title: Fair infrastructure allotment
subtitle: Quotas tied to headcount and taxes — a harder bargain
choose-if: cable_neg_infra_cap = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.cableNegEnsureApi()
Q.cable_neg_infra_cap = 2
Q.cableNegReprisalAddEach(Q.CABLE_NEG_REPR_INFRA_FAIR_EACH)
!}
go-to: terms_menu

@prior_leverage_demands
title: Demands from earlier leverage
view-if: cable_neg_prior_leverage = 1
subtitle: Only on the table if we already had corp leverage before the rupture

If we had real leverage over a megacorp before the cable break, we can spend it on non-security terms.

- @demand_education_enroll: Enroll corp employees' children in city schools
- @demand_education_pay: Corps pay for that education
- @demand_land_tax: Land tax on corp holdings for general revenue
- @terms_menu

@demand_education_enroll
